**For you to decide:** whether to tell the RG authors. I found no published Solar System test of their covariant theory, so this would be new to them, and contacting them is outward-facing.

**So what?** This changes a pending decision and gives a result about someone else's published theory. It doesn't move the count of 6 or Bucket 0. One open thread is untested: no standard scalar–tensor theory seems able to produce a density-dependent permittivity, since the field only shifts by about (Φ/c²)/(3+2ω). If that holds, density-keyed gravity would have no covariant theory behind it at all.

